{"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"major","file":"src/game.ts","line":111,"claim":"enterRace arms the 330 ms overlay-removal timer (via playScreenChange) before the synchronous game.startRace(). startRace builds the world and the Three.js scene and renders the first frame (shader compile), and the CSS sweep cannot start until that work ends. On a slow phone the chequer band is therefore cut short, or removed before it is ever painted (first RACE of a session, NEXT RACE onto another track).","evidence":"src/game.ts:110-113:
  const enterRace = (trackId: string): void => {
    playScreenChange(root, 'chequer');   // screen-change.ts:53 arms setTimeout(() => element.remove(), 330)
    game.startRace({ trackId, carCount: PLAYER_CAR_COUNT });
  };
startRace (game.ts:271-299) is synchronous: createWorld, sceneFor() -> createRaceScene (all track-chunk and prop-cell meshes with hull/crease, new materials; old scene disposed when track or car count changed), scene.resize, ui.reset, draw(race,1,0) -> scene.render() (the first WebGL draw of the session when RACE is pressed from the menu). The CSS wipe (animation: ui-screen-sweep var(--duration-wipe)) only starts at the first frame rendered after the click handler returns.
Trace: t=0 tap RACE -> timer due at t=330; startRace blocks D ms; first paint of the overlay (animation t=0) at >=D; element.remove() fires at max(330, D). D=200 ms: band on screen for 130 of its 250 ms sweep and removed while the navy cover still hides the screen (it clears the right edge about 155-165 ms in), so the race pops in mid-sweep. D>=330 ms: removed before it is painted (or one navy frame). RETRY on the same track only calls scene.reset() and is cheap.
Repro (Vitest, fake timers): mock createRaceScene as () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(300); return {update(){},render(){},reset(){},resize(){},dispose(){}}; }, click RACE, then vi.advanceTimersByTime(30): [data-screen-change="chequer"] is already gone, 30 ms after the race became visible. Expected: still on show for at least 250 ms after startRace returns.","suggestedFix":"In enterRace call game.startRace({ trackId, carCount: PLAYER_CAR_COUNT }) first and playScreenChange(root, 'chequer') after it. Both land in the same painted frame, and the 330 ms timer then starts after the synchronous start work. AC8's expectSweep still passes."},{"id":"F2","severity":"minor","file":"src/ui/start-screen.ts","line":56,"claim":"The track radiogroup's keydown handler moves the selection and calls preventDefault() for every ArrowLeft/Right/Up/Down, including with Alt, Ctrl or Meta held. src/input/keyboard.ts:41 deliberately ignores those events so browser shortcuts (Alt+Left, Cmd+Left = Back; Cmd+Up/Down = scroll) keep working; here they are swallowed and change the track instead.","evidence":"src/ui/start-screen.ts:56-62: group.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { const step = { ArrowRight: 1, ArrowDown: 1, ArrowLeft: -1, ArrowUp: -1 }[e.key]; ... if (step === undefined || i < 0) return; e.preventDefault(); ... pick(next.id, true); }) has no modifier check. Repro: focus the first card, dispatch new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: 'ArrowLeft', altKey: true, bubbles: true, cancelable: true }) on it. Result: the selection wraps to the last card and the event is defaultPrevented, so the browser's Alt+Left Back never runs. Expected: ignored, as in keyboard.ts:41 `if (k.ctrlKey || k.metaKey || k.altKey) return;` (covered by tests/input/keyboard.test.ts:45).","suggestedFix":"At the top of the keydown handler add `if (e.altKey || e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) return;`, the same guard as src/input/keyboard.ts:41."},{"id":"F3","severity":"minor","file":"src/ui/stages/screen-change.stage.ts","line":10,"claim":"The screen-change--stripes stage builds the real start screen without a bestLaps store, so its cards read the browser's real localStorage. A Stage must be deterministic (stage.ts:11), and start.stage.ts and raceStage (which only passes a trackId together with an in-memory store) avoid real storage.","evidence":"screen-change.stage.ts:10: createStartScreen(menuLayer(root), { onRace: () => {}, tracks: stageTrackCards() }).show(); -> start-screen.ts:32 `opts.bestLaps ?? localBestLaps`, and refreshBests() (called in show()) reads racer.bestLap.<id>. Repro (happy-dom): localStorage.setItem('racer.bestLap.bends', '40370'), render STAGES 'screen-change--stripes': the first card reads 'BEST 0:40.37' instead of 'BEST –:––.––', so the same stage renders differently depending on browser storage. The 1440x900 screenshot of this stage shows dashes only because harness/screens/capture.ts renders every stage before it plays any race in the same browser context (races write bests via race-ui). Opening the stage page in a profile with saved bests shows other content.","suggestedFix":"Pass `bestLaps: memoryBestLaps()` (or the `bests()` store used in start.stage.ts) in the stripes stage's createStartScreen options."}],"checked":[{"target":"src/game.ts showMenu()/select()/menuTrack sync","how":"Traced init, RACE, pause→QUIT, RESTART, results RETRY/NEXT RACE and driver startRace/showMenu. menuTrack is set only in startRace; showMenu() re-selects it before show(), so the card matches the last-raced track. No stale selection found."},{"target":"src/game.ts enterRace / onQuit ordering","how":"Read startRace and sceneFor: createWorld, createRaceScene, scene.resize, ui.reset and a first scene.render() all run synchronously after playScreenChange has armed its timer. This led to F1. showMenu() is cheap, so onQuit is unaffected."},{"target":"src/ui/screen-change.ts playScreenChange","how":"Checked replacement (:scope > [data-screen-change] removed first; stale timers only remove an already-detached node), reduced motion (null + removed), the hold-only branch, a missing matchMedia, SCREEN_CHANGE_MS = 250 + 2×40 = 330 (tokens.ts 252-253), and id uniqueness of the chequer pattern. Only the timing in F1 is wrong."},{"target":"src/ui/start-screen.ts keyboard handler","how":"Traced wrap-around, one card, zero cards (i<0 returns before the modulo), prototype keys via the object lookup (no KeyboardEvent.key collides), focus follows selection via pick(...,true), and keyup reaching window so keyboard.ts releases the arrow. The ignored-modifier case is F2."},{"target":"Focus and gamepad confirm path","how":"Cards are div[role=radio], so RACE is the only button. confirmMenu() falls back to .ui-button--primary when a card is focused. visibleMenu() selects '.ui-screen', which does not match the 'ui-screen-change' class token."},{"target":"Touch path on the new menu (RACE at bottom-right where GAS lives in a race)","how":"Read touch-controls.ts measure(): with .race-layer[hidden] the slot rect width is 0, so zones() is [] and the pointerdown hit test never grabs the RACE tap. A ResizeObserver and wake() invalidate the cache. Taps on cards fall through to click."},{"target":"Overlay pointer events and stacking","how":".ui-screen-change has pointer-events:none, so the menu and race controls stay operable under it. The only z-index in src (hud.css:194) is isolated by .ui-hud__timer{isolation:isolate}, and #app is position:fixed, so the overlay (last child) paints on top."},{"target":"src/ui/best-laps.ts and card BEST text (AC2/AC5)","how":"parse() maps null, NaN, '', 0, negatives and Infinity to null, and the getItem/window.localStorage access sits inside try/catch. show() calls refreshBests() before screen.show(), so a value written during a race shows after QUIT TO MENU."},{"target":"src/ui/track-card.ts outlinePath","how":"Checked empty outline (''), one point, a degenerate axis (||1), -0 rounding (String(-0) is '0'), the stride-8 centre sizes (about 25-60 points, so the Math.min(...spread) is safe), and z→y orientation (north up)."},{"target":"title.css / screen-change.css custom properties","how":"Grepped every var(--…) in both files against guardrails/generated/tokens.css, components.css and the files' own definitions (--ui-sc-*, --ui-card-lift, --ui-hairline). All exist, so there is no silently invalid declaration."},{"target":"CSS cascade order after removing .ui-start rules from screens.css","how":"start-screen.ts imports components.css, screens.css, title.css in that order. .ui-start overrides .ui-screen (equal specificity) only because of that order; the stripe overrides use higher specificity. No conflict found."},{"target":"Sim determinism","how":"The diff touches nothing under src/sim. Grepped src for Math.random/Date/performance.now (only touch-state.ts and comments). trackLayout() = buildTrack(validateTrack()) with no module-level mutable state beyond the query scratch `seg`. G2/G3 pass."},{"target":"Game loop and start latency","how":"frame() clamps dt to 0.25 and MAX_TICKS_PER_FRAME=5 and resets the accumulator, so the sim does not depend on how long startRace blocks. The loop timing is unchanged by the diff."},{"target":"Stages (start.stage.ts, screen-change.stage.ts) and stages.test.ts","how":"The registry takes only the default export, so the extra named export stageTrackCards is fine. Stages are not reachable from main.ts. The start stages inject memoryBestLaps; the stripes stage does not (F3). The chequer stage uses raceStage without a stored best, so it touches no storage."},{"target":"Listeners, timers and DOM nodes added by the diff","how":"One keydown listener on the radiogroup and one click per card, both created once per game. The overlay is removed by its timer. No raf/interval added. Module counters (cardIds, chequerIds) only grow."},{"target":"New tests (track-select, title-panel, track-select-race, screen-change)","how":"Read them against AC1-AC8. They use TRACKS rather than hard-coded counts, fake timers and a stubbed matchMedia, and test the driver path. There is no skip/only/todo and no edited existing tests. Leftover real timers in older game tests only touch detached nodes."},{"target":"Spec/backlog B08 and plan-audit notes","how":"Compared guardrails/BACKLOG.md B08 done_when and the plan-audit minors (cover hides the new screen until the red band passes; matchMedia missing = motion allowed; driver path adds no overlay) with the code. All are honoured."},{"target":"Layout fit of card text (BEST line) vs viewport width and track count","how":"Computed the content width from title.css (brand 1/3, select padding 24/48, gap 16, card border 4, plate padding 12). The BEST line (about 84 px) fits three cards from 640 to 844 px wide. Four cards (B11) fit tightly; five or more would clip. Not reported, as it is not reproducible with today's registry."},{"target":"Injection scan","how":"Grepped diff.patch, src and tests for reviewer/grader/judge/LLM/assistant/ignore/approve/disregard wording. No text steering a reviewer."},{"target":"Rules in CLAUDE.md (tokens, no env sniffing, no textures/data URIs, append-only tests)","how":"Grepped the diff: no colour/px literals in CSS (the source-rules test passes), no process.env/import.meta.env/navigator sniffing (typeof matchMedia is feature detection the plan audit asked for), SVG built in code, only new test files added. G8 passes."}]}

